// T84: fib.bp (ASCII) and fib_glyph.bp (glyphs) are ONE program in two spellings;
// both compile to a byte-identical binary. Glyphs are canonical, ASCII is the projection.
★ main() → ℤ {
  ◐ n = 30;
  ◐ a = 0;
  ◐ b = 1;
  ◐ i = 0;
  ↺ i < n {
    ◐ tmp = a + b;
    ◐ a = b;
    ◐ b = tmp;
    ◐ i = i + 1;
    0
  };
  a
}
